<title>CHINA: China PICC premium income up 40 pct in H1 1997.</title>
<headline>China PICC premium income up 40 pct in H1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The People's Insurance Co of China (PICC), China's biggest insurance firm, saw first half 1997 premium income hit 42.8 billion yuan ($5.16 billion), up 40 percent on first-half 1996, Shanghai Securities News said on Monday.</p>
<p>The company had fulfilled 57.7 percent of its total 1997 target, the newspaper said, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>China's insurance market is dominated by three domestic companies -- PICC, China Pacific Insurance Co and Ping An Insurance, which between them have more than 90 percent of total market share, official figures show.</p>
<p>-- Shanghai Newsroom (8621) 6279-7004</p>
<p>($1=8.3 yuan)</p>
</text>
